Problem:
In parsers/lay_parser.py, _clean_compact_value() applies boundary regexes that include unqualified terms like:

File(?:\b|_)
Template(?:\b|_)
ObjId
PosId

Because these terms are not qualified as real compact serialized keys, legitimate sequence names can be corrupted.

Example input:
Seq.1.NameInput_File_SequenceSeq.1.Cnt1

Bad behavior:
Parsed sequence name may truncate to:
Input

Correct behavior:
Parsed sequence name must remain:
Input_File_Sequence

Boundary truncation must only fire for real serialized compact keys, such as:
- Seq.1.Name
- Seq.1.Cnt
- Seq.1.ReadOnly
- Seq.1.Item.1.ObjId
- Seq.1.Item.1.PosId
- Labware.1.Id
- Labware.1.DefSeqValid
- Labware.1.File
- Labware.1.Template
- Labware.1.SiteId
- Labware.1.LwProperties.1.Property
- Labware.1.LwProperties.1.Value
- Layer.1.2.SeqName
- Layer.1.2.LabwareName

Required fix:
1. Remove unqualified File, Template, ObjId, and PosId from generic compact value truncation boundaries.
2. Replace them with key-qualified boundaries only:
   - Seq.<n>.Name
   - Seq.<n>.Cnt
   - Seq.<n>.ReadOnly
   - Seq.<n>.Item.<i>.ObjId
   - Seq.<n>.Item.<i>.PosId
   - Labware.<n>.Id
   - Labware.<n>.DefSeqValid
   - Labware.<n>.File
   - Labware.<n>.Template
   - Labware.<n>.SiteId
   - Labware.<n>.LwProperties.<i>.Property
   - Labware.<n>.LwProperties.<i>.Value
   - Layer.<layer>.<slot>.SeqName
   - Layer.<layer>.<slot>.LabwareName
3. Do not truncate ordinary sequence names containing:
   - File
   - Template
   - ObjId
   - PosId
4. Keep rejecting truly malformed overcaptured names containing actual embedded structural keys.
5. Preserve previous hotfix behavior:
   - malformed overcaptures like long Seq.1.Item... strings are rejected.
   - valid Hamilton sequence names remain accepted.
